            <ArticleTitle>Harvesting the inferior epigastric artery through a transverse suprapubic incision.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1749-50</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The inferior epigastric artery has been used as an alternative arterial conduit in coronary artery bypass graft surgery. Its harvesting requires a single or double, long abdominal paramedian incision that is technically difficult and does not yield a good cosmetic result. We describe an alternative new approach to one or both inferior epigastric arteries through a transverse suprapubic cosmetic incision.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
